    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0573" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">339.115 General Motors Export Co./9:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-19T19:00:00-05:00">April 19, 1935—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Reference Department’s telegram No. 10 April 19, 6 p.m.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d488-f1"/> Penn Tobacco Company has communicated further with the
                    Department referring to the urgent cable received today from Marcus<anchor
                        n="3a" xml:id="d488-f2"/> and requesting that you “cable full confidential
                    report from Marcus on situation with reason for his request”. You are authorized
                    to cable such message.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d488-f1" n="3" xml:id="d488-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d488-f2" n="3a" xml:id="d488-f2-content">
                <p>Manager of Dominican Tobacco Company.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
